Register, unregister, and list program objects.

usage: @program register <id> <image> [ram]
       @program unregister <id>
       @program list

A program object (programs/<id>) names an RV32 ELF image that @run and the
verb dispatcher launch. @compile produces one from source; @program is the
manual counterpart for an image that was already built.

register
  Bind programs/<id> to an existing image. If <image> begins with '/' it is
  an absolute VFS path and the in-world filesystem must hold that file;
  otherwise it is a host image relative to the image directory
  (vm.image_path), which must hold that file. [ram] is the guest RAM in
  bytes, 0 or omitted for the default. Re-registering an id switches it
  between a host and a VFS image cleanly. The object persists across
  restarts.

unregister
  Delete programs/<id> from the store.

list
  Show the registered programs and the image each is bound to.

The program id is a single name with no '/'. Wizard only: a launched
program runs code with its owner's authority.

Examples:
  @program register tool /bin/tool.elf
      Bind programs/tool to a VFS image.
  @program register hello hello.elf
      Bind programs/hello to a host image under the image directory.
  @program list
  @program unregister tool

See also @compile, @run, help programs.
